      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://warrencountyil.gov/communities/roseville/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Originally called Hat Grove, the village adopted the name Roseville in 1853 as it grew.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roseville%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Chicago, Burlington and Quincy Railroad arrived in the 1860s, opening a trade corridor that linked Roseville to St. Louis and beyond.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roseville%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Roseville incorporated as a village on May 8 1875, formalizing its local government after decades of informal growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roseville%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Village Hall and Fire Station share a single building downtown, a historic reminder of early 20th‑century municipal cooperation.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
